  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Mrs Funny tried to weigh her baby Jessica, but as the baby would not keep still she had to resort to other methods. She held Jessica while her older daughter, Melissa, read the scale to be 72 kg. Then Melissa held Jessica while Mrs Funny read the scale as 48 kg. Finally Mrs Funny held Melissa, while baby Jessica read the scale as 102 kg.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the combined weight of Mrs Funny, Melissa and Jessica.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$111\\text{ kg}$",
          "worked": "Let $F$, $M$ and $J$ be the weights in kilograms of Mrs Funny, Melissa and Jessica respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}F+J&=72 &&\\text{(1)}\\\\M+J&=48 &&\\text{(2)}\\\\F+M&=102 &&\\text{(3)}\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdd (1), (2) and (3):\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2(F+M+J)&=72+48+102\\\\2(F+M+J)&=222\\\\F+M+J&=111\\end{align*}$$\n\nTheir combined weight is $111\\text{ kg}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the weight of baby Jessica?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$9\\text{ kg}$",
          "worked": "Substitute $F+M=102$ from (3) into the total found in part a:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}J&=111-102\\\\J&=9\\end{align*}$$\n\nJessica weighs $9\\text{ kg}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
